Description: aic8800_fdrv: the wiphy may be moved into another network namespace
 Without WIPHY_FLAG_NETNS_OK, 'iw phy <phy> set netns' is refused, so the interface can't
 be used from a namespace (as test rigs do to pair two radios in one box). The driver
 keeps nothing per namespace: its only uses of init_net are its own netlink control
 socket and an optional bridge lookup.
Author: NomDeTom
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-21
---
--- aic8800.orig/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
+++ aic8800/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
@@ -9226,7 +9226,8 @@ if((g_rwnx_plat->usbdev->chipid == PRODUCT_ID_AIC8801) ||
         WIPHY_FLAG_HAS_CHANNEL_SWITCH |
         #endif
         WIPHY_FLAG_4ADDR_STATION |
-        WIPHY_FLAG_4ADDR_AP;
+        WIPHY_FLAG_4ADDR_AP |
+        WIPHY_FLAG_NETNS_OK;
 
     #if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(3, 16, 0)
     wiphy->max_num_csa_counters = BCN_MAX_CSA_CPT;
